      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean yeah i get that nothing is officially \"disclosed\" but think about it... the sensors for hrv (heart rate variability) are already there. if you have access to gait and heart rhythm data, you can literally predict mood or stress levels. isn't it technically possible for them to be running those algorithms in the background without it being part of the \"official\" fitness app features? it feels like a massive loophole for data collection if they wanted to.",
